WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.819
Frozen warmed enough hearts that critics and
young audiences alike just couldn't seem to

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.320
let it go.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.870
Luckily for Disney, it looks likes critics
are mostly feeling the same way about the

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.839
film's upcoming sequel, Frozen II.

00:00:11.839 --> 00:00:15.549
The long-anticipated follow-up to what was
once the highest-grossing animated movie of

00:00:15.549 --> 00:00:20.010
all time had its star-studded premiere in
Los Angeles on Thursday, November 7.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:24.570
A movie six years in the making, the latest
enchanting adventure of sisters Anna and the

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.510
Snow Queen Elsa saw Hollywood creatives and
entertainment critics come out in droves to

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.000
get the first look at the film.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.840
While the enchanting fantasy flick — which
follows the sisters as they and their friends

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.090
travel far from the kingdom of Arendelle to
find the source of Elsa's powers — isn't

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.780
slated for release until November 22nd, critics
in attendance have already taken to social

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.740
media to share their initial reactions.

00:00:45.740 --> 00:00:49.100
And it all seems to point to yet another animated
hit for Disney.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.340
“You can't just follow me into fire."

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:53.300
"Then don't run into fire."

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.920
The general consensus from those with premiere
invites point to a follow-up that's creatively

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.149
competitive with the original, a film that
quickly became both an award-winning animated

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:04.520
classic and pop cultural phenomenon.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.260
Frozen II's songs and visuals especially have
received considerable praise.

00:01:08.509 --> 00:01:12.920
Mashable deputy entertainment editor Angie
J. Han acknowledged that the Frozen sequel

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.580
exists in part simply because of the financial
success of the first film.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.620
Still, Han said that doesn't take away from
what the second installment does right.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:23.840
Among these things are new songs and an adorable
new character.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.719
Jason Guerrasio, Business Insider's senior
entertainment reporter, called Frozen II "a

00:01:28.719 --> 00:01:31.780
worthy sequel" that offers up some truly amazing
animation.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:32.380
He added:

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:35.100
"Elsa rides a water horse and it's breathtaking.

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.600
The song 'Into the Unknown' is primed to be
'Let It Go'-like addictive (sorry parents)."

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:44.080
When the social embargo for Frozen II lifted
after the film's screening, critic Clayton

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:49.680
Davis took to Twitter and shared how profoundly
impacted he was by the film's messages, particularly

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.640
as a father watching with his daughter.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:56.420
"#Frozen2 embarks as not just an evolution
of its characters, but it sincerely acknowledges

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.540
that its fanbase has grown over the last
6 years, and they have new things to learn

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.420
in a changing world.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.640
Songs are plentiful.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.080
Beautiful shots at times.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.820
It was something I REALLY needed."

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:10.810
It's a level of emotional resonance Alisha
Grauso, an editorial lead at Atom Tickets,

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:12.280
said actually brought her to tears.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:16.820
Part of that emotional reaction was due to
the film's focus on female empowerment, for

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.470
which the original was also praised.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:19.860
She tweeted after seeing the film,

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.860
"#Frozen2 is breathtakingly beautiful and
leans in on empowerment for its characters.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.140
I cried at least 3 times.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:31.330
From the story to the last thread on Elsa's
dress, the care and love put into it shows.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:35.860
And, good news, every one of Team Elsa gets
at least one solo this time around."

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.120
“I might cry.”

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.079
“Go ahead, I won't judge."

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.660
The DisInsider's editor-in-chief Skyler Shuler
went perhaps the farthest of any other journalist,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:49.900
proclaiming that the Elsa, Anna, Kristoff,
Olaf, and Sven reunion was better than the

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:51.360
record-smashing Frozen.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.080
Schuler even provided a warning for parents
who are still getting over the infectious

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.300
love of "Let It Go."

00:02:56.660 --> 00:03:00.560
"I can't believe I am saying this, but FROZEN
2 is better than its predecessor.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.200
Darker, a little more mature, but still an
excellent film for families, the songs believe

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.700
it or not are catchier, so parents beware."

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:12.660
Still, some critics have noted that Frozen
II's plot and other elements simply don't

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.390
stand up to those of its predecessor, although
they don't have a completely flipped opinion.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.060
"Wait, what am I looking at right now?

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:20.260
Why are you hanging off the earth like a bat?"

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.940
Among the critics who have been, well, more
critical of Frozen II is Alison Foreman.

00:03:24.959 --> 00:03:28.780
Another Mashable reporter in attendance at
the premiere, Foreman gave the film props

00:03:28.780 --> 00:03:32.460
despite it not having the same magic of the
first movie, at least in her eyes:

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.580
"Just got out of #Frozen2!

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:39.430
It doesn't capture all the magic of the first,
but it's got: Elsa in a wetsuit, Anna ugly

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:45.020
crying, Sven ugly crying, Kristoff singing
a '90s rock ballad, Olaf at his wisest, and...

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.020
THIS GOOD BOY!!

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.980
(We must protect him at all costs.)"

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.380
For critics like Scott Menzel, the editor-in-chief
of We Live Entertainment, Frozen II couldn't

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.320
quite reach the quality delivery of the 2013
movie.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:00.600
"Frozen 2 loses some of the magic of the original
but its soundtrack is surprisingly superior.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.590
Kristoff, Sven, &amp; Olaf standout even though
the script leaves Anna &amp; Elsa out in the cold.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.459
It is a decent sequel but definitely a step
down from the first."

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:14.269
Ashley Menzel, who's part of the Los Angeles
Online Film Critics Society, echoed those

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:18.850
feelings, stating that the animated production's
shift in its target demographic actually hurts

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:19.380
the movie:

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.720
"Frozen 2 creates musical magic, but story
wise, doesn't quite reach the level of the

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.260
original.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:28.960
Olaf is certainly the highlight of the film
&amp; brings much needed levity to a pretty dark

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:29.500
film.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:32.660
It feels like it is for a much older crowd
than the target demo."

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.620
"Ooooh that's a rough business to be in right
now.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.480
I mean, that is really… that's unfortunate."

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:43.040
Still, almost all the reviews find something
to praise about the film, and it sounds like

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.940
Disney just might have another billion-dollar
box office smash on its hands.

